Totally optional, but this would be easier to read with a local `struct` definition, like:

```suggestion
	struct RenameMap {
		const char *from;
		const char *to;
		const char *profile;
	};
	const RenameMap renames[] = {
		{ "/user/hand/left/input/grip_surface/pose", "/user/hand/left/input/palm_ext/pose", nullptr },
		{ "/user/hand/right/input/grip_surface/pose", "/user/hand/right/input/palm_ext/pose", nullptr },
```

... especially in the loop further down with all the `i + x` indexing

You can get the number of elements at compile time via:
```
constexpr size_t length = sizeof(renames) / sizeof(renames[0]);
```
... to replace the stopping on `nullptr` thing

